                "turmeric",
                "allspice",
                "cinnamon",
                "sugar",
                "water"
            ],
            "recipe_steps": {
                "1": "Rinse the lentils and place them in a saucepan with plenty of water.",
                "2": "Bring to a boil and simmer for 12–15 minutes, until tender but not falling apart. Drain and set aside.",
                "3": "Peel the onions and slice them thinly.",
                "4": "Place the onions in a large flat plate, add the flour and 1 tsp salt, and toss well to coat.",
                "5": "Heat the sunflower oil in a large saucepan over medium-high heat. / Test the oil with a small piece of onion; it should sizzle vigorously.",
                "6": "Fry about ⅓ of the onions at a time for 5–7 minutes, stirring frequently, until golden brown and crisp.",
                "7": "Remove with a slotted spoon and drain on paper towels. Sprinkle lightly with salt.",
                "8": "Repeat with the remaining onions.",
                "9": "Wipe out the saucepan, leaving a little oil behind.",
                "10": "Add the cumin and coriander seeds and cook over medium heat for 1–2 minutes, stirring, until fragrant.",
                "11": "Add the rice, olive oil, turmeric, allspice, cinnamon, sugar, ½ tsp salt, and a generous amount of black pepper.",
                "12": "Stir well to coat the rice with the spices.",
                "13": "Add the cooked lentils and 3½ dl water.",
                "14": "Bring to a boil, cover, and simmer over very low heat for 15 minutes.",
                "15": "Remove from the heat, lift the lid, place a clean kitchen towel over the pot, replace the lid, and let stand for 10 minutes.",
                "16": "Gently fold half of the fried onions into the rice and lentils.",
                "17": "Transfer to a serving dish and top with the remaining fried onions."
            },
